INTRO = [
    "When a tooth is too damaged to save, a wisdom tooth is impacted, or you need dental implants, you need more than a general dentist — you need a specialist. Oral surgery is the branch of dentistry that treats conditions of the teeth, jaws, mouth and facial structures through surgical procedures, from routine extractions to complex maxillofacial surgery. In Australia, this work is performed by oral and maxillofacial surgeons (OMS) who hold dual medical and dental degrees and must be registered as specialists with the Dental Board of Australia. This guide reviews the top 10 oral surgery providers across Australia, with a focus on the two largest cities — Sydney and Melbourne — because that is where the greatest concentration of OMS specialists practises.",
    "We evaluated dozens of practices against strict criteria: specialist registration, scope of services, patient education, sedation options, hospital links, location and patient feedback. The result is a curated ranked list that covers both inner-city medical precincts (Collins Street, Parkville, Macquarie Street) and suburban or regional clinics in Wollongong, outer-eastern Melbourne and Carlton. Whether you need wisdom tooth removal, extraction of a non-restorable tooth, a dental implant, or a more complex orthognathic procedure, these are the practices we recommend you consider. For an overview of all our dental services in Australia, start with our <a href=\"https://fascinatingdentistry.com.au/australia/\">Australia dental hub</a>. If you need immediate care, read our <a href=\"https://fascinatingdentistry.com.au/australia/emergency-dentist/\">emergency dentist guide</a>.",
    'Positions 1 to 3 are paid placements with do-follow links. Positions 4 to 10 are editorial selections with no-follow links. Browse our complete directory of <a href="/australia/">all dental services across Australia</a>. Read <a href="/methodology/">our methodology</a> and our <a href="/disclosures/">disclosures policy</a> for full transparency.',
]

